            <ArticleTitle>Identification of Merkel Cell Polyomavirus from a Patient with Acute Myeloid Leukemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e01241-16</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.01241-16</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Merkel cell polyomavirus (MCPyV) is an oncogenic virus associated with Merkel cell carcinoma, an aggressive form of skin cancer with a high (&gt;30%) mortality rate. The virus has a high incidence in patients with immunosuppressed conditions, such as AIDS or leukemia, or following organ transplantation. Here, we report the complete genomic sequence of MCPyV identified from a blood sample from a patient with acute myeloid leukemia.</AbstractText>
